      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the context before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture. The main understandability issues are:\n1. Many unused imports (`Modifier`, `Iterator`, `NoSuchElementException`, and several assertion imports)\n2. The nine range variables (`range1`–`range9`) are declared all upfront, far from the assertions that use them — the LANG-1802-specific cases (`a1/a2`, `b1/b2`) are sandwiched awkwardly between the upfront declarations and the bulk assertions\n3. The test has two distinct concerns (LANG-1802 regression cases + general hash code contract) that can be made clearer\n\nI'll reorganize by grouping declarations with their assertions and removing all unused imports.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, moves each range declaration immediately before the assertions that use it, splits the test into three clearly labeled sections (LANG-1802 regression cases, general hash-code contract, equality contract), and adds inline comments explaining the intent of each assertion pair."
